NELS:88 follows a nationally representative cohort of eighth graders throug=
h 2000, linking baseline test performance to later educational attainment. =
The public-use data identify students=92 tenth-grade high schools, allowing=
 peer distributions and outcomes such as bachelor=92s-degree completion to =
be constructed for roughly 10,500 students. The main limitation is that the=
 sampled students may not fully represent each high school=92s complete coh=
ort.

