sv?rlkey=3D3jat69by82t2rteuzi7k25eiz&dl=3D0
HS&B:80 follows nationally representative cohorts of high-school sophomores=
 and seniors, linking baseline test performance and school membership to la=
ter educational attainment. The public-use data support school-by-cohort pe=
er distributions for roughly 23,000 students, with binary outcomes such as =
college attendance and bachelor=92s-degree completion by 1986. Its main lim=
itation is that the two cohorts have different follow-up horizons, so they =
should be analyzed separately.




