Using Cursor currently you can have multiple threads going simultaneously w=
ith multiple, even different LLM models (open, sonnet, grok, Claude, etc.) =
but those threads are distinct.  Separating the research domains has kept t=
he threads at a manageable length and focused, avoiding early appearance of=
 hallucinations.  I have created inventive ways for them to communicate via=
 .md files but it is primitive and slow.  I have seen a lot of stuff online=
 about folks who are creating new products, platforms, etc. to allow them t=
o collaborate in real time.  I have purposely not investigated that to main=
tain focus.  So, as you dabble and become Agentic-fluent, please be on the =
lookout for something that allows us to have our sub-agents collaborate in =
real time.
